From: TDVP <tdvp@example.invalid>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 16:20:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] tdvp: hide the unavailable microphone control

The Raspberry Pi plugin creates separate buttons for output and microphone
levels. T-Display K230 only exposes a usable output route; PulseAudio still
reports a monitor source, which makes the upstream input button visible with
an incomplete microphone icon. Keep the upstream output control and all of
its popup, mute and device-selection behaviour, but never expose the input
button on TDVP.

Signed-off-by: TDVP <tdvp@example.invalid>
---
 src/commongui.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/commongui.c b/src/commongui.c
index 4d5dbe9..a79c2dd 100644
--- a/src/commongui.c
+++ b/src/commongui.c
@@ -154,6 +154,18 @@ void update_display (VolumePulsePlugin *vol, gboolean input)
 {
     const char *icon;
 
+    /*
+     * K230 has no user-facing capture path. PulseAudio nevertheless exposes
+     * the output monitor as a source, so upstream would show a second,
+     * non-actionable microphone button. Keep the maintained output widget
+     * unchanged and suppress only that unavailable input endpoint.
+     */
+    if (input)
+    {
+        gtk_widget_hide (vol->button[1]);
+        gtk_widget_set_sensitive (vol->button[1], FALSE);
+        return;
+    }
     pulse_count_devices (vol, input);
     if ((!input || !vol->wizard) && vol->pa_devices + bluetooth_count_devices (vol, input) > 0)
     {
-- 
2.47.1
